    "media:imagetext": "RADIO\nDATE\nGMT\nFREQ. MHZ\nRST\n2 WAY\nJOSEPH E. SINGLETON, W40PZ\n200 N. CHRISTMAS HILL ROAD\nTITUSVILLE, FL 32780\n***************\nThis radio amateur is one of the proud\nthousands of present, retired, or former\nemployees of Pan American Airways.\n*\n***\n*\n*\n*******\n*\n*\nXMTR\nRCVR_\nXCVR\nAMPL\nPOWER\nANT\nPicture: Reproduction of a painting by\nJohn T. McCoy showing a Martin M-130\nFlying Boat about to land on Hong Kong\nHarbor in 1936. Three of these aircraft\nwere built. The most famous,\nnamed\n\"China Clipper,\" was used to inaugurate\nthe first commercial Trans-Pacific flight by\nPan American Airways in 1935.\nOPAN AM\n\"For over 50 years\nAmerica's airline to the world\"\n*\n*\n***\n*\n*\n*\n*\n*\n*\nRemarks:\nBREVARD COUNTY",
